## 🗄️ Real-World Database Classification

| Category | What It Chooses | Databases | Use Case |
|----------|----------------|-----------|----------|
| **CP** | Consistency + Partition Tolerance | MongoDB, HBase, Redis (cluster), Zookeeper | Banking, inventory, booking systems |
| **AP** | Availability + Partition Tolerance | Cassandra, DynamoDB, CouchDB | Social media feeds, analytics, DNS |
| **CA** | Consistency + Availability | Traditional RDBMS (PostgreSQL, MySQL single-node) | ⚠️ Only works on a single node (no partition possible) |

> **CA is a trap answer!** If there's no partition (single machine), CAP doesn't apply. The moment you go distributed, P is forced, so CA doesn't exist in distributed systems.

### How Each Category Behaves During a Partition

